---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import record from '../../data/homeboard-release.json';
import {validateRelease} from '../../../scripts/homeboard/validate-release.mjs';
const release = validateRelease(record, process.cwd());
const size = (release.sizeBytes / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1) + ' MiB';
---
<Base title="Homeboard TV — Download for Android TV & Google TV" description="A household command center with cooking timers, event alarms, rain, calendar, air quality and favorite apps. Download Homeboard TV and get started.">
<main class="homeboard">
<nav><a class="brand" href="/">bioHACK · NET</a><a href="/">All projects ↗</a></nav>
<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your TV, your home screen</p><h1>Homeboard TV</h1><p class="intro">Your house’s command center, on your Android TV or Google TV.</p><p class="features">Rain forecasts · Calendar · Air quality<br/>Timers &amp; alarms · Groceries · World clocks<br/>Phone configuration · Wallpaper providers</p><div class="links"><a href="#install">Install on your TV ↓</a><a href="https://github.com/wbniv/homeboard-tv">Source code ↗</a></div></div>
<aside class="download"><span class="chip">Early release · APK download</span><h2>For Android TV &amp; Google TV</h2><p>Android 8.0 or newer. Try Homeboard from your apps before choosing a default launcher.</p><a class="button" href={release.downloadUrl} download>Download APK · {size}</a><p class="metadata">Version {release.versionName} · {release.publishedDate}</p><p>Free · No account required</p><a href="#verify">Release notes &amp; verification ↓</a></aside></section>
<figure><a href="/homeboard/images/dashboard.png"><img src="/homeboard/images/dashboard.png" width="1920" height="1080" alt="Homeboard dashboard showing hourly rain, calendar, air quality, world clocks and YouTube in Favorites"/></a><figcaption>Actual TV capture · 0.1.74 · Fresh test dashboard with YouTube in Favorites.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="timers"><figure><a href="/homeboard/images/timers.png"><img src="/homeboard/images/timers.png" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Expanded Timers and alarms on Cast1, showing named cooking timers, remaining times and direct controls"/></a><figcaption>Actual Cast1 capture · Demonstration timers.</figcaption></figure><div><h2>Every dish. The next thing to do.</h2><p>Run named cooking timers together. Set a one-off alarm for a date and time, such as calling a ride or leaving the house.</p><p>Pause, add a minute and stop from the TV or paired phone. Start with a compact 2×1 widget; press OK for all the controls.</p><p>Grant alarm access on the TV. Sound over other apps needs a powered, audible TV. Test a short timer on your TV before relying on it.</p><a href="https://github.com/wbniv/homeboard-tv/blob/main/docs/how-to/timers-and-alarms.md">Timers &amp; alarms guide ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="lower"><div id="install"><h2>Install on your TV</h2><ol><li>Download the APK on your phone or computer.</li><li>Transfer it to your TV using a USB drive, where supported, or a TV file-transfer app.</li><li>Open it with a TV file manager. Allow <strong>Install unknown apps</strong> for that file manager, install, then turn that permission off.</li><li>Open <strong>Homeboard TV</strong> from your apps.</li></ol><p>Menu names and transfer methods vary by TV. You can try Homeboard without changing your default launcher.</p><div class="links"><a href="/homeboard/guide/">User guide ↗</a><a href="/homeboard/guide/quick-start.pdf">Printable PDF ↗</a></div><p class="companion">Optional TV cleanup uses a separate computer companion. The APK download provides the TV dashboard. See the <a href="https://github.com/wbniv/homeboard-tv/blob/main/docs/how-to/tv-cleanup.md">companion setup guide</a> for its current requirements and limits.</p></div>
<div id="verify"><h2>Updates &amp; release details</h2><p>Install newer public versions from this page over the existing public app to retain settings. If Android rejects an update, keep the installed app to preserve its dashboard and settings. Check that you downloaded a newer public release, rather than the separate debug build.</p><p class="notice">Testing Homeboard already? The public app is separate from the debug test app. Its settings do not transfer automatically.</p><details open><summary>Release {release.versionName}</summary><ul>{release.notes.map(note=><li>{note}</li>)}</ul></details><details><summary>Known limits</summary><p>This early release has been tested on Chromecast devices. Other Android TV devices may differ. Internet access is needed for fresh rain and air-quality data. Coverage and timestamps are shown in the app. Some wallpaper providers require separate apps or accounts. English and Thai are supported; translation review continues.</p></details><details><summary>Verify the download</summary><p>Package: <code>{release.packageId}</code><br/>Size: {release.sizeBytes.toLocaleString('en-US')} bytes</p><p>APK SHA-256</p><code>{release.sha256}</code><p>Signing certificate SHA-256</p><code>{release.certificateSha256}</code><p><a href={release.downloadUrl.replace(/[^/]+$/, 'SHA256SUMS')}>Download checksums</a> · <a href={release.sourceArchiveUrl}>Exact source snapshot</a></p><p>Base source commit: <a href={`https://github.com/wbniv/homeboard-tv/commit/${release.sourceCommit}`}>{release.sourceCommit.slice(0,12)}</a>. The source snapshot includes the release version and any changes recorded during the build.</p></details></div></section>
<footer>Independent project based on <a href="https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv">CleanYourTV</a> · <a href="/homeboard/LICENSE.txt">MIT license</a> · <a href="/homeboard/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt">Third-party notices</a><p>For support and source, visit <a href="https://github.com/wbniv/homeboard-tv">Homeboard TV on GitHub</a>.</p></footer>
</main>
</Base>
<style>
.timers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;gap:28px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:28px}.timers figure{margin:0}.timers p{font-size:16px}.homeboard{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:30px 36px;color:var(--ink)}nav{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);padding-bottom:20px}.brand{letter-spacing:3px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink)}a{color:#7dd3fc}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #f7cb72;outline-offset:5px}.eyebrow{color:#7dd3fc;letter-spacing:2px;font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:30px 0 8px}h1{font-size:60px;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-2px;margin:12px 0 20px}h2{font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 14px}p{margin:0 0 18px}.intro{font-size:20px;max-width:600px;color:#c7c6c3}.hero,.lower{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start}.features{color:#c7c6c3}.download{padding:24px;background:#23252a;border:1px solid #3c4049;border-radius:16px;margin-top:32px}.download p,.lower p{font-size:14px}.chip{color:#b9e6c3;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase}.button{display:block;padding:16px;background:#7dd3fc;color:#101b22;border-radius:9px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;text-decoration:none;margin:18px 0 10px}.button:hover{background:#b7e9ff}.metadata{color:#b7bdc8}.links{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}figure{margin:28px 0}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #444;border-radius:12px}figcaption{font-size:12px;color:#b6b5b0;margin-top:8px}.lower{border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-top:28px}ol{padding-left:23px;margin:0}li{padding:0 0 9px 5px}details{border:1px solid #42454c;border-radius:9px;padding:12px 15px;margin-bottom:15px}details p{margin-top:14px}summary{cursor:pointer}details ul{margin:16px 0 0;padding-left:1.4em;list-style:disc}details li{padding-left:.25em}code{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--rule);margin-top:30px;padding:20px 0;font-size:12px;color:#bbb}.notice{border-left:3px solid #c68a47;padding-left:14px;color:#e2cfb5}.companion{margin-top:20px;color:#c7c6c3}@media(max-width:650px){.timers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;gap:28px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:28px}.timers figure{margin:0}.timers p{font-size:16px}.homeboard{padding:22px}.hero,.lower{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}.timers{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:45px}.intro{font-size:18px}.download{margin-top:12px}nav{font-size:13px}.eyebrow{margin-top:25px}.lower{gap:28px}}
</style>
